 content="""
Based on feedback and comments in the Fedora tickets

[1](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2326283),
[2](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2383375),
[3](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2383751),
[4](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2387561),

I propose these changes to the action file:

- Set `pipefail` to not cushion etckeeper's return code
- Use the `goal_resolved` hook instead of `pre_base_setup` to allow non-root usage of `dnf` and avoid (costly) `etckeeper` runs for `dnf` actions not installing or removing any package. Not sure if that is the best choice. Looking at the [DNF5 workflow](https://dnf5.readthedocs.io/en/latest/dnf5_workflow.html), a hook between 22.8 and 22.9, i.e., after user approval would be nice. Open to suggestions.
- Pass `dnf`'s PID to `etckeeper`'s `post-install.d/50vcs-commit` to allow for better commit subjects via `ETCKEEPER_PARENT_COMMAND_LINE`. This needs another patch for `post-install.d/50vcs-commit` though, to actually use that information.

With that, the action file would look like

```sh
# to be placed in /etc/dnf/libdnf5-plugins/actions.d
# requires dnf5 5.2.11.0 or later
goal_resolved:::raise_error=1:/usr/bin/sh -o pipefail -c /usr/bin/etckeeper\ pre-install\ \|\ /usr/bin/sed\ -e\ 's/^/log.INFO=/'
post_transaction::::/usr/bin/sh -o pipefail -c ETCKEEPER_PPID=${pid}\ /usr/bin/etckeeper\ post-install\ \|\ /usr/bin/sed\ -e\ 's/^/log.INFO=/'
```

and patching `post-install.d/50vcs-commit` so that the relevant part looks like this (allowing to pass an `ETCKEEPER_PPID` from the outside):

```sh
if [ -z \"${ETCKEEPER_PPID}\" ]; then
	# Find the pid whose parent is the command line that the user ran.
	# Depending on how the highlevel package manager starts etckeeper,
	# this can be either the parent process, or the parent of the parent
	# process.
	case $HIGHLEVEL_PACKAGE_MANAGER in
		pacman|zypper|dnf)
			ETCKEEPER_PID=\"${PPID}\"
		;;
		apt|yum)
			# (Only procps ps is currently supported, others will fail,
			# so this may end up empty.)
			ETCKEEPER_PID=$( ps --no-headers -o ppid \"${PPID}\" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^ *//' )
		;;
	esac

	if ! [ -z \"${ETCKEEPER_PID}\" ]; then
		# Find the parent to get the command line.
		# (Only procps ps is currently supported, others will fail,
		# so this may end up empty.)
		ETCKEEPER_PPID=$( ps --no-headers -o ppid \"${ETCKEEPER_PID}\" 2>/dev/null | sed 's/^ *//' )
	fi
fi

if ! [ -z \"${ETCKEEPER_PPID}\" ]; then
	ETCKEEPER_PARENT_COMMAND_LINE=$( ps --no-headers -o args \"${ETCKEEPER_PPID}\" )
fi
```

Note that for the old DNF plugin we carried a patch anyway, hence I moved it in the `pacman|zypper` branch, see [this ticket](https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2203408).

Would such a patch be acceptable, @joey ?

"""]]
